---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { socialImage } from '../lib/media.js';
import { breadcrumbLd } from '../lib/seo.js';
import { NON_AFFILIATION_LONG, REPOSITORY_URL, repositoryFileUrl } from '../site.js';

const meta = {
  title: 'Licence',
  description:
    'gcportrait is open source under the MIT License: what you may do with it, what stays reserved (its name and icon), third-party material and Google’s trademarks.',
  path: '/licence/',
  socialImage: socialImage('licence', 'gcportrait’s licence: MIT'),
  jsonLd: [breadcrumbLd([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Licence', path: '/licence/' }])],
};
---

<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT -->
<Base meta={meta}>
  <div class="container prose licence">
    <h1>Licence</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      gcportrait’s own work, its code, its texts and its images, is licensed under the MIT License
      (<code>MIT</code>). Copyright © 2026 Florian Chrometz.
    </p>
    <p>
      The licence text is <a href={repositoryFileUrl('LICENSE')}>LICENSE</a> in the repository (also at
      <a href="/licenses/gcportrait-LICENSE.txt">gcportrait-LICENSE.txt</a> on this site). Every source file names the
      licence in its first lines with the line <code class="code-long">SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>What you may do</h2>
    <p>
      Use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense and sell gcportrait, run it for yourself or for others,
      on its own or as part of your own software or services, commercially or not. The one condition: the copyright
      notice and the permission notice stay with every copy or substantial portion of it. It comes without warranty.
    </p>
    <p>
      The licence asks nothing of an instance you run, modified or not. The app still links its source in its footer on
      every page, “Source (MIT)”, as a courtesy to the people who use an instance: it points at this project’s
      repository by default, and an instance that runs a modified version can point it at its own source (the backend’s
      <code>SOURCE_URL</code>, <a href="/docs/configuration/">configuration reference</a>).
    </p>

    <h2>The gcportrait name and icon</h2>
    <p>
      The gcportrait name and the gcportrait icon are not covered by the MIT License. They identify this project and may
      not be used to present other software or services as gcportrait or as endorsed by it; forks must use their own
      name and icon.
    </p>
    <p>
      The icon is <code>brand/icon.svg</code> and every rendering of it: the favicons, this website’s logo and the app’s
      mark, the wordmarks, and the mark on the link-preview images. The details are in
      <a href={repositoryFileUrl('brand/LICENSE.md')}>brand/LICENSE.md</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party material</h2>
    <p>Third-party material keeps its own licences and terms and is not covered by the MIT License:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>npm dependencies</strong>, each under its own licence. Only licences that do not reach gcportrait’s own
        combined work are allowed (permissive licences and the file-scoped MPL-2.0), and a check enforces that on every
        change; the list is <a href={repositoryFileUrl('THIRD_PARTY.md')}>THIRD_PARTY.md</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The Roboto fonts</strong> the app and this website use, self-hosted, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1
        (<a href="/licenses/roboto-LICENSE.txt">Roboto</a>, <a href="/licenses/roboto-mono-LICENSE.txt">Roboto Mono</a>).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Cloud product icons</strong>, vendored unmodified and used under Google’s icon usage terms
        (<a href={repositoryFileUrl('packages/icons/README.md')}>packages/icons</a>). They are trademarks, not code, and
        the MIT License does not cover them.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Licence texts</strong> under <code>scripts/licenses/</code>, kept verbatim.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Contributions</h2>
    <p>
      Contributions are accepted under the MIT License, the licence gcportrait is offered under (inbound = outbound);
      there is no contributor licence agreement. The <a href="/contributing/">contributing page</a> has the rest. The
      source is on <a href={REPOSITORY_URL}>GitHub</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Google trademarks</h2>
    <p>{NON_AFFILIATION_LONG}</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .licence {
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }
</style>
